# Pro-étale Cohomology, Chapter 1: Introduction

The source section consists of the aims of the book, historical and
bibliographical discussion, motivation for the pro-étale topology, and a
high-level roadmap.  It does not introduce a standalone definition, identity,
diagram, exact sequence, example, hypothesis, or theorem interface.

The statement that the small pro-étale site has enough quasi-compact
w-contractible objects is a roadmap assertion: the notions involved are
introduced and developed in later sections.  Recording it here would require
either importing later material or inventing an interface before its
definitions, so it is intentionally accounted for in this section's
documentation rather than duplicated as a declaration.
